   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1792236298564,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Where each thing lives\n\u2022 Doubts, pins, notes, highlights, quiz ticks, watched chapters: only in krayon.marks.v1 (browser), mirrored as part of one blob to users/local-user/state/study. No per-item backend API.\n\u2022 Explain longer: the only interaction that reaches the backend and Gemini. The new segment replaces the old one in the segment doc and in the lesson (krayon.course); the old version is kept only in rounds/<n>.\n\u2022 Sync: the browser is the source of truth. The backend copy restores data after the browser is cleared; two tabs or devices overwrite each other. uid is hardcoded to local-user. \"Clear resources\" (POST /api/admin/reset) wipes both.\n\u2022 The /ws \"regenerate\" message handler exists in the backend but the frontend uses the HTTP endpoint.",
   "originalText": "Where each thing lives\n\u2022 Doubts, pins, notes, highlights, quiz ticks, watched chapters: only in krayon.marks.v1 (browser), mirrored as part of one blob to users/local-user/state/study. No per-item backend API.\n\u2022 Explain longer: the only interaction that reaches the backend and Gemini. The new segment replaces the old one in the segment doc and in the lesson (krayon.course); the old version is kept only in rounds/<n>.\n\u2022 Sync: the browser is the source of truth. The backend copy restores data after the browser is cleared; two tabs or devices overwrite each other. uid is hardcoded to local-user. \"Clear resources\" (POST /api/admin/reset) wipes both.\n\u2022 The /ws \"regenerate\" message handler exists in the backend but the frontend uses the HTTP endpoint.",
   "fontSize": 15,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "rec-0346",
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "baseline": 90,
   "autoResize": false
  }
